From 9ac1a0b75575bb436e3222d245b1c7b76ed38db4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Fabian=20Gr=C3=BCnbichler?= <f.gruenbichler@proxmox.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Jul 2022 12:43:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] handle namespaced features
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

cargo will now inject a feature named after an optional dependency (and
use it on the RHS of the feature definition) if needed, so we don't need
to do it manually here. if no such feature exists it means that all
references to the optional dependency are namespaced with 'dep:' prefix,
and that the dependency itself should not(!) be exposed as feature.

any features depending on such a prefixed optional dependency will still
caused the required `Depends:` to be generated, we just skip the
corresponding `Provides:` for the no-longer-usable pseudo-feature.

tested various combinations using the local crate support, they all seem
to do the right thing. it might be prudent to write test cases for all
combinations we expect to handle.

Signed-off-by: Fabian Grünbichler <f.gruenbichler@proxmox.com>
---
 src/crates.rs | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/crates.rs b/src/crates.rs
index f3f9d7d..b1a6a0b 100644
--- a/src/crates.rs
+++ b/src/crates.rs
@@ -477,14 +477,11 @@ impl CrateInfo {
             features_with_deps.insert(feature.as_str(), (feature_deps, other_deps));
         }
 
-        // calculate dependencies of this crate's "optional dependencies", since they are also features
+        // calculate required dependencies for implicit no-default-features
         let mut deps_required: Vec<Dependency> = Vec::new();
         for deps in deps_by_name.values() {
             for &dep in deps {
-                if dep.is_optional() {
-                    features_with_deps
-                        .insert(dep.name_in_toml().as_str(), (vec![""], vec![dep.clone()]));
-                } else {
+                if !dep.is_optional() {
                     deps_required.push(dep.clone())
                 }
             }
